Here is a sample hitchance system that you can use for your League of Legends spell casting system:

1. Calculate the time difference between the current and old paths. This will give you an idea of how much the enemy has changed its path over time.
2. Calculate the distance between the current and old paths. This will give you an idea of how much the enemy has moved over time.
3. Calculate the angle between the current and old paths. This will give you an idea of how much the enemy has turned over time.
4. Combine the time difference, distance, and angle to create a hitchance value between 0.1 and 1. A value of 1 means that the enemy will definitely stay on its current path, and a value of 0.1 means that it is very unlikely to stay on its current path.

Here is some sample code that you can use to calculate the hitchance value:
```
float CalculateHitchance(Path currentPath, Path oldPath)
{
    float timeDifference = (currentPath.Count - oldPath.Count) / (float)currentPath.Speed;
    float distance = Vector2.Distance(currentPath[0], oldPath[0]);
    float angle = Vector2.Angle(currentPath[0] - oldPath[0], Vector2.UnitY);

    // Combine the time difference, distance, and angle to create the hitchance value
    float hitchance = timeDifference + distance + angle;

    return hitchance;
}
```
You can then use this hitchance value to decide whether to cast the spell or not. For example, you can set a threshold of 0.5, and if the hitchance value is greater than 0.5, you can cast the spell.
```
if (CalculateHitchance(enemyCurrentPath, enemyOldPath) > 0.5f)
{
    // Cast the spell
}
else
{
    // Preserve the spell
}
```
